FINAL ANSWER:
Git history can't tell you who the right reviewers are. It also can't confirm that the original authors are still around, because it only shows when they last committed.

**Who owns what**
- `.github/CODEOWNERS` has one line, `* @google/go-uuid-contributors`. There are no per-file owners. I can't see that team's membership from here, so check it on GitHub.
- There is no `sql.go` any more. It was renamed to `database_sql.go` in cfc4a55 (2025-03-10), and `git log` for that file lists Ravi Menon as the only author.

**Who wrote the code and when they were last active**

| Area | Original authors | Last commit by them | Recent maintainers |
|---|---|---|---|
| `time.go` | Paul Borman (6 commits), plus Bryan Matsuo, Martin Lindhe, MikeWang, Youngjae Lee, Nicu Micle | Youngjae Lee, 2024-06; Nicu Micle, 2024-11 | Sam Okafor (2025-04), Alexander Rowe (2025-02) |
| `version7.go` | MikeWang (2), David Kaufman, Alex Bozhenko, Andreas Deininger | MikeWang, 2024-07; Bozhenko, 2024-07 | Mei Chen (2025-08), Ravi Menon (2026-05) |
| SQL (`database_sql.go`, formerly `sql.go`) | David E. Wheeler, Andrew Stone, Justin Overfelt, Daniel Souza, Paul Borman, Steven Kaufman | Kaufman, 2021-01; Borman, 2021-07 | Ravi Menon, rename only |
| `null.go` | Paul Borman, Samuel Roth | 2021-07 | none |

**Are the original authors still around?**
- The SQL code was written in 2015–2021 by contributors who haven't committed since. Paul Borman's last commit under his own address was in 2021-07. A `bormanp` account committed on 2023-10-26, so he may still be involved.
- I can't tell whether any of them would respond.
- `time.go` and `version7.go` were written by occasional contributors, and none of them has committed since 2024 (the `time.go` authors) or mid-2025 (`version7.go`).
- Ravi Menon is the most active person in the history: 7 commits since 2024, the latest on 2026-06-17.
- Alexander Rowe is also active (latest commit 2026-03-09). The history shows this person under several identities: Alexander Rowe, Alex Rowe and `arowe`. I'm assuming those are one person, but I haven't confirmed it.
- Noor Haddad (2025-07), Mei Chen (2025-08) and Sam Okafor (2025-05) have gone quiet in the last year.

**My suggestion**
- Ask **Ravi Menon** first for all three areas. They have touched every one of them and are the most recent committer. For `time.go` and `version7.go`, add **Alexander Rowe**, who added `UnixMillis` for v7.
- For SQL, nobody active wrote the code, so Ravi Menon is the best reviewer, not a domain expert. Treat Paul Borman as someone to consult on the original design, not as a reviewer.

**Oddities**
- Kofi Mensah's commit d97a7fa has a 1970-01-01 timestamp. That's a bad date, and they don't show up elsewhere in the history. It may be worth checking where that commit came from.
- Earlier authors of `time.go` and the SQL code mostly used personal addresses, so I'd need GitHub to see who's active in other ways, like issues, PR reviews and merges. `gh` could check that if you want me to.

